{"abstract":[{"text":"A place in a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" that a consumer can stop waiting on and come back","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to, keeping every value sent in between.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make one with the subject’s "},{"code":"makeSubscription()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It subscribes when it is made, exactly like the subject’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator: a "},{"code":"CurrentValueSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s subscription starts with the current value, and every value sent after that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is buffered for it, without limit, until "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"},{"type":"text","text":" returns it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The difference is cancellation. Cancelling a task waiting in an iterator’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"text":" ends that iterator’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subscription and discards its buffer. Cancelling a task waiting in a subscription’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","type":"reference"},{"text":" throws","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"text":" from that call only: the subscription stays subscribed, and a later ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","type":"reference"},{"text":" returns the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values sent before and after the cancellation, in order. That suits a consumer that runs in rounds, such as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch run that is cancelled and started again, and must not miss what was sent between rounds.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The subscription unsubscribes when its last copy is released. It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncIteratorProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":", so an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operator can read it through "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncIteratorSequence"},{"type":"text","text":"; a cancelled read then ends that operator’s run with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"type":"text","text":" and leaves the subscription for the next run."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Example","text":"Example","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let events = PassthroughSubject<String>()","let subscription = events.makeSubscription()","","let firstRound = Task { try await subscription.next() }","firstRound.cancel() \/\/ Throws CancellationError from that wait; nothing is lost.","_ = await firstRound.result","","events.send(\"launch\")","events.send(\"login\")","let first = try await subscription.next()  \/\/ \"launch\"","let second = try await subscription.next() \/\/ \"login\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Wait on a subscription from one task at a time. A call to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"},{"text":" made while another call on the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subscription is waiting throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/ConcurrentNext"},{"text":", and the waiting call carries on as if it hadn’t been made.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Afluent"}],"externalID":"s:7Afluent19SubjectSubscriptionV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubjectSubscription"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubjectSubscription.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription.swift#L40"},"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"SubjectSubscription"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/ConcurrentNext"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/AsyncIteratorProtocol-Implemen